# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 040
# Act: EVA+  (Evaluation aimed at Figure)   Stance: Binding   Site: Lens
#
# EVA's pass for the "anomalous" kind: witnessing turn-38's two claims
# against a general, the same discipline turn-25/turn-26 held for the
# absence-recurrence kind. The general here is the SAME negative control
# (kernel/data/noise-control.json) — legitimately reused, because it was
# built to answer exactly this question (does this construction, with
# nothing planted, produce the sign in question) for both kinds it was
# checked against: turn-32 already reports its magnitude check at -0.10
# aperture-widths, INSIDE its own ground, sign "ordinary."
#
#   claim(@cc38c3ae... "signal (magnitude-anomaly)") vs noise-control (-0.10 widths, "ordinary"): witnessed
#   claim(@186c8ea0... "signal (magnitude-anomaly)") vs noise-control (-0.10 widths, "ordinary"): witnessed
#
# Each witnessing checked independently against the one committed control.
# If noise-control's own value had also read "anomalous," neither claim
# above would be witnessed — the construction would be incapable of
# distinguishing planted anomalies from its own ordinary variation, the
# same vacuous-ground failure turn-25 named for the absence kind.
